From 7fae564272cc78d79b9bfa848ec83195fb6d2a7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 15:10:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07193/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-12: real live-path
 A/B -- no capability win, real cost

Answers the question REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-11 left open: does SGE actually
help on the real (non-stripped) live path?

Added CARNOT_ARC_SGE_CANDIDATE_ROUTER=1 env-var escape hatch
(_sge_candidate_router_requested(), mirroring CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_
INDUCTION's pattern) since a subprocess-based measurement can't
monkeypatch the in-process module flag.

New scripts/arc_sge_live_path_ab.py: both arms construct genuinely
full-production E3AgentPolicy(game, proposer=None) -- real induction,
frame-change scorer, goal-bias, the actual SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG
defaults, NOT outer_loop_sge_smoke_test.py's stripped harness.
Differs ONLY in candidate_router. Scored via arc_leaderboard_eval.py's
own run_game() (the real leaderboard scorer, zero reimplementation).

Ran on sp80, budget=250. Both arms: levels=0, reached=L0, actions=241,
efficiency=0.0 -- byte-identical outcome, identical gap signature.
SGE took 165.4s vs the discriminative router's 42.9s: ~3.9x slower
for zero measured difference. Notably, even the SHIPPED DEFAULT never
leaves level 0 on sp80 at this budget -- confirming REQ-ARC-FCP-
5699-6's router-independence finding on the real production path,
not just the offline diagnostic harness.

Per SUBMITTED_SGE_CANDIDATE_ROUTER_ENABLED's own docstring ("re-
enable only after a real matched-budget A/B... shows a win"), this
result doesn't meet that bar -- the flag stays False. This closes
the REQ-ARC-FCP-5699 chain's central open question with an honest,
real-path-verified no, on the one game tested.

1 new test (env var flips SGE on without touching the module
default) + spec-declaration test. Spec: REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-12 with its
own scenario.

